  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Thursday...\n\nConditions will be warm and mostly dry today with highs generally\nin the 70s. \n\nLate this evening through Saturday, a Pacific shortwave moves \nthrough the region, bringing another round of scattered showers \nand isolated thunderstorms and dropping highs into the 60s\nSaturday. The best chance (60-80%) for any showers or storms is \neast of Billings, where PWATs are expected to be around 120-150% \nof normal and CAPE values around 200-500 J/kg. No strong storms \nare expected.\n\nSunday into next week will see warm and dry conditions return to\nthe region with highs in the upper 70s and 80s. A disturbance\nmoving through northern Montana early Monday will bring \nwidespread breezy winds out of the north of 20 to 40 mph. With \nthe warm and dry conditions ongoing, any areas that have not \nrecently received precipitation will have an increased concern \nfor grass fires. \n\nThrough the rest of the week, an occasional shortwave in the flow\nmay bring a low (less than 30%) chance for precip but no \nwidespread events are anticipated. Archer",
